<% content_for :title, "IFS | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-ifs-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-ifs-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-ifs-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-ifs-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / IFS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>WHO THE</span>
        <span>FUCK IS</span>
        <span>TALKING?</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-ifs-intro">
        YOU HAVE PARTS.<br>
        NONE OF THEM ARE ALL OF YOU.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- BASIC IDEA -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-pink">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      01 / THE BASIC IDEA
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        YOU ARE<br>
        NOT ONE<br>
        THING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Internal Family Systems, or IFS, looks at the mind as having
        different parts — different patterns, reactions, emotions,
        beliefs, and ways of trying to protect you.
      </p>

      <p>
        One part wants to get your shit together.
        Another wants to disappear. One wants connection.
        Another wants everyone to leave you the fuck alone.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-callout">
        <p>
          HAVING CONTRADICTORY PARTS<br>
          DOESN'T MAKE YOU A CONTRADICTION.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- SELF -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-yellow">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      02 / SELF
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        WHO'S<br>
        BEHIND THE<br>
        NOISE?
      </h2>

      <p>
        In IFS, Self is the grounded place from which you can notice
        your parts without immediately becoming consumed by them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Self is associated with qualities like curiosity,
        compassion, calm, clarity, confidence, courage,
        creativity, and connection.
      </p>

      <p>
        You don't have to feel perfectly calm to access Self.
        Sometimes the first sign of Self is simply being able to say:
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-big-question">
        HUH.<br>
        WHAT'S GOING<br>
        ON HERE?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- IDENTIFY THE PART -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-purple">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      03 / FIND THE PART
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        WHO JUST<br>
        TOOK THE<br>
        FUCKING WHEEL?
      </h2>

      <p>
        When your reaction feels intense, automatic, familiar,
        or completely out of proportion to what's happening,
        get curious before you start fighting yourself.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-questions">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What am I feeling right now?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Where do I feel it in my body?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What does this part want me to do?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What does it believe will happen if I don't?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>What is it trying to protect me from?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PROTECTORS -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-black">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      04 / PROTECTORS
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        EVERYBODY'S<br>
        GOT A<br>
        FUCKING JOB.
      </h2>

      <p>
        IFS assumes that even the parts causing problems are usually
        trying to accomplish something.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-part-grid">

        <div>
          <h3>THE CONTROLLER</h3>
          <p>
            Tries to keep everything organized, predictable,
            and under control so nothing can go wrong.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THE CRITIC</h3>
          <p>
            Attacks you first because it thinks criticism might
            prevent rejection, failure, or humiliation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THE ESCAPER</h3>
          <p>
            Wants relief immediately. Numb it, avoid it,
            leave it, distract from it — anything but feel it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THE ANGRY ONE</h3>
          <p>
            Uses anger to protect boundaries, vulnerability,
            fear, hurt, or powerlessness.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THE IMPULSIVE ONE</h3>
          <p>
            Wants the reward, relief, excitement, or escape
            right fucking now.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>THE PERFECTIONIST</h3>
          <p>
            Believes being flawless might finally make you
            safe from failure or judgment.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        These aren't official personality types you need to fit into.
        They're examples. Your parts may look completely different.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- UNBLENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-pink">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      05 / UNBLENDING
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        STEP<br>
        THE FUCK<br>
        BACK.
      </h2>

      <p>
        When a part completely takes over, IFS calls that being
        blended with the part.
      </p>

      <p>
        Unblending doesn't mean making the feeling disappear.
        It means creating enough distance to notice that the feeling
        is happening without treating it as your entire identity.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="ifs-tool-label">BLENDED</p>
          <p>I AM FUCKING FURIOUS.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="ifs-tool-label">UNBLENDING</p>
          <p>A PART OF ME IS REALLY FUCKING ANGRY.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Tiny wording change. Huge difference.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- GET CURIOUS -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-yellow">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      06 / GET CURIOUS
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        ASK BEFORE<br>
        YOU FUCKING<br>
        ATTACK.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Instead of immediately trying to shut a part up,
        argue with it, or get rid of it, ask what it's doing.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-questions">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What are you afraid would happen if you stopped doing this?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What are you trying to protect me from?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>When did you learn that this was necessary?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What do you need me to understand?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>What would help you trust me enough to step back a little?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- POLARIZATION -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-purple">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      07 / POLARIZED PARTS
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        INTERNAL<br>
        TUG OF<br>
        WAR.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Sometimes two parts are pulling in completely opposite directions.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-conflict">

        <div>
          <p>I NEED TO GET MY SHIT TOGETHER.</p>
        </div>

        <span>VS.</span>

        <div>
          <p>I CAN'T FUCKING DO THIS ANYMORE.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Or one part wants connection while another wants isolation.
        One wants sobriety while another desperately wants relief.
        One wants to spend money while another is terrified about money.
      </p>

      <p>
        Instead of deciding one part is good and the other is bad,
        ask what each side is afraid will happen if the other side wins.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ADDICTION / IMPULSES -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-black">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      08 / URGES
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT DOES<br>
        THIS PART<br>
        WANT?
      </h2>

      <p>
        When an urge shows up — drinking, getting high, spending,
        shopping, escaping, blowing something up, or doing something
        impulsive — you can examine the function of the urge without
        automatically obeying it.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-flow">

        <p>WHAT DO I WANT TO DO?</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>WHAT WOULD THAT GIVE ME RIGHT NOW?</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>RELIEF? ESCAPE? CONTROL? EXCITEMENT? NUMBNESS?</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>WHAT IS THE PART TRYING TO PROTECT ME FROM?</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>CAN I MEET THAT NEED WITHOUT DOING THE THING?</p>

      </div>

      <div class="ifs-tool-callout">
        <p>
          UNDERSTANDING THE PART<br>
          DOESN'T MEAN LETTING IT DRIVE.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ACCOUNTABILITY -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-pink">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      09 / ACCOUNTABILITY
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        COMPASSION<br>
        ISN'T A<br>
        FREE PASS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Understanding why a part did something does not erase
        the consequences of what happened.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can understand the fear, pain, anger, or desperation
        underneath a behavior and still take responsibility for
        the behavior itself.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-big-question">
        I CAN UNDERSTAND<br>
        WHY I DID IT<br>
        AND STILL OWN<br>
        THAT I DID IT.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BIPOLAR -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-yellow">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      10 / IFS + BIPOLAR
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        PARTS<br>
        AREN'T<br>
        EPISODES.
      </h2>

      <p>
        IFS can be useful for exploring your internal reactions,
        conflicts, beliefs, and coping patterns.
      </p>

      <p>
        But mania, depression, mixed episodes, and psychosis are not
        simply "parts" that need to be listened to or unblended from.
        Bipolar disorder involves mood episodes that may require
        psychiatric and medical treatment.
      </p>

      <div class="ifs-tool-callout">
        <p>
          IFS CAN BE A TOOL.<br>
          IT DOESN'T REPLACE BIPOLAR TREATMENT.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PRACTICE -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-section ifs-tool-purple">

    <div class="ifs-tool-number">
      11 / TRY IT
    </div>

    <div class="ifs-tool-content">

      <h2>
        WHO'S<br>
        TALKING<br>
        RIGHT NOW?
      </h2>

      <div class="ifs-tool-workbook">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>NOTICE</h3>
          <p>What am I feeling or wanting to do?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>SEPARATE</h3>
          <p>Can I say "a part of me feels..." instead of "I am..."?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>ASK</h3>
          <p>What is this part trying to accomplish?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>LISTEN</h3>
          <p>What is it afraid would happen if it stopped?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>RESPOND</h3>
          <p>What does this part actually need from me?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>CHOOSE</h3>
          <p>What do I want to do now that the part isn't making the decision alone?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="ifs-tool-ending">

    <p class="ifs-tool-ending-small">
      LISTEN TO YOUR PARTS. YOU DON'T HAVE TO HAND THEM THE KEYS.
    </p>

    <h2>
      GET CURIOUS.<br>
      STEP BACK.<br>
      THEN CHOOSE.
    </h2>

    <p>
      The loudest voice in your head doesn't automatically
      get to make the decision.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "ifs-tool-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>